.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt LOCALEDEF 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm localedef
.Nd compile a bounded POSIX locale definition into the runtime catalog
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl i Ar input
.Fl f Ar charmap
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility parses a bounded POSIX locale definition and charmap and writes the runtime catalog
image read by
.Xr gencat 1
and the RavenBSD locale catalog runtime
.Pq magic Sq ff88ff89 .
The six locale categories become catalog sets 1 through 6; the
.Dq LOCALE
set 7 records the optional name, the charmap name, the charmap entry count and the list of
categories present.
.Pp
Supported categories are
.Sy LC_CTYPE , LC_NUMERIC , LC_TIME , LC_COLLATE , LC_MONETARY
and
.Sy LC_MESSAGES .
Each category starts with its name, contains
.Ic keyword Ar \(dqvalue\(dq
lines and ends with
.Sy END
followed by the category name.
.Ic copy Ar \(dqC\(dq
and
.Ic copy Ar \(dqC.UTF-8\(dq
are recorded. Values are quoted strings with
.Sq \e\e ,
.Sq \e\(dq ,
.Sq \en ,
.Sq \et
and
.Sq \er
escapes; a
.Sq ;
separated list is stored joined by
.Sq ; .
Comments start with
.Sq # .
.Pp
The charmap supports
.Sm off
.Ic <symbol> /xHH U+HHHH Op name ...
.Sm on
lines. Comments start with
.Sq #
or
.Sq % ;
at least one entry is required.
.Pp
Unsupported categories, keywords, charmap lines and malformed values are errors. The image is
built in memory and written only after the whole source and charmap parse, so a failure never
leaves a partial catalog as a success.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar input
Read the locale definition from
.Ar input .
.It Fl f Ar charmap
Read the charmap from
.Ar charmap .
.It Fl o Ar output
Write the catalog image to
.Ar output .
Without
.Fl o
the image goes to standard output.
.It Fl c
Create the output. Accepted for POSIX compatibility; the tool always creates it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success; 1 for a malformed or unsupported source, a charmap error or an I/O failure; 2 for
an invalid command line.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gencat 1 ,
.Xr locale 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD bounded subset of POSIX.1-2024.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
The target binary is a host-only stub, like
.Xr gencat 1 .
The source subset is listed in
.Pa docs/posix/P4-simple3.md ;
copied locale data is recorded, not expanded, and the charmap is validated but not compiled into
a code-set table.
